# Wegscheider cycle consistency and ideal-mixture Gibbs equilibrium
# (thermo-equilibrium focus).
#
# Cycle consistency: a closed three-step cycle with equilibrium
# constants K = [2, 1/2, 1] has product of numerators 2 and product of
# denominators 2 — the cycle is thermodynamically consistent, and the
# std.chemistry pack's cycle_consistent cell admits with the exact
# zero delta. An inconsistent cycle (e.g. K = [2, 1, 3]) refuses typed
# CycleInconsistency(residual d) with the exact witness difference.
#
# Gibbs: the ideal-mixture free energy along the extent xi of
# 2 H2 + O2 -> 2 H2O is minimized through the existing goal path
# (minimize wrt xi); the stoichiometry vector nu = [2, 1, -2] is
# certified by the existing mass_balance cell, so conservation is
# automatic along xi.
# Run: emath check language/examples/chemistry/thermo-equilibrium.emath
package std

emath field_pack chemistry:
    exports:
        cell balance
        cell mass_balance
        cell graph_rewrite_preserve
        cell cycle_consistent
    metadata:
        description Wegscheider cycle consistency plus Gibbs equilibrium via generic goal path
